{
  "_doc": "Where the castle's entity NPCs are on the game clock (sim_core::npcs::RoutinesFile; RoutinePlan::pose). points: named spots on walkable ground (yaw: facing once there); a point `door:<class id>` is that class's door. routines: per ghost, staff member, shopkeeper and clerk, steps sorted by game time `at`: at that time the NPC sets off from the previous step's point (the last step's, for the first) for `to` along the NPC nav graph (no moving staircase flight, no hidden passage; its own house's rooms for ghosts and students) at rules.walk_speed_mps (ghosts ghost_speed_mps), then stands there (anim idle or sit) until the next step; `hidden`: gone (the server removes the entity) until the next step. The walk must fit before the next step (checked). A shopkeeper or a clerk has one step (where it stands). students: the generator's rules (lead_mins before a session they set off for its door, hidden through it; bed and rise; bed_walk_mins to reach the night point) and per student its classes, idle point (idle_anim) and night point. The seventh floor is an island of the NPC graph (only moving flights reach it): ghost_house_a stays there. Tune points so the walks look right in game. docs/architecture.md 'NPCs'.",
